## Entry Animation

When `animated={true}`, bars grow from zero width to their full D3-scaled width on first load, staggered one after another (top to bottom). The animation uses design tokens from the `enterAnimation` collection via the shared `useEntryAnimation` hook. After the entry settles, subsequent data changes animate smoothly using `transitionAnimation` tokens via `useDataTransition`.

See **[HorizontalBarGroup Entry Animation](./HorizontalBarGroup.md#entry-animation)** for implementation details.

## Data Transition Animation

When `animated={true}` and data changes after the chart has loaded, bars smoothly transition from their current widths to new widths using a staggered wave pattern (top to bottom). The transition uses design tokens from the `transitionAnimation` collection via the shared `useDataTransition` hook.

See **[HorizontalBarGroup Data Transition](./HorizontalBarGroup.md#data-transition-animation)** for implementation details.

### Usage

```tsx
const [data, setData] = useState(dataSetA);

<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  animated={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{ chartTitleValue: 'Revenue' }}
/>

// When data changes, bars smoothly transition to new widths
<button onClick={() => setData(dataSetB)}>Switch Data</button>
```

## Design Tokens Used

| Property      | CSS Custom Property                                    | Description                                              |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Container Gap | `var(--HorizontalBarChart-gap, var(--Spacing-5))`      | Gap between chart sections (two-layer pattern)           |
| Bar Group Gap | `var(--HorizontalBarGroup-gap, var(--Spacing-3))`      | Gap inside `HorizontalBarGroup` (content wrapper / X-axis) |
| Bar Color     | `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-{n})`                  | Categorical palette token from DataVis CSS pipeline      |
| Bar Height    | `var(--Spacing-2)` – `var(--Spacing-7)`                | Resolved from the `barHeight` T-shirt size via a fixed map in the `HorizontalBar` leaf (`XS`→`--Spacing-2` … `2XL`→`--Spacing-7`); not a consumer-overridable two-layer variable |

## Legend Auto-Generation

When `chartLegend` is `true` and no `chartLegendConfig.items` are provided, the component uses `chartLegendConfig.categoryLabelValue` for a single-series legend, or auto-generates up to 6 items from `data` (one per unique custom `color`, or a single item from the first data point when no custom colors are set). See ChartLegend documentation for details.

## Height Behavior

The `height` prop controls the **total chart height**, not just the bar group. The HorizontalBarGroup automatically stretches to fill the remaining space after header, legend, DataDisplay, and footer.

### How It Works

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ChartHeader (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartLegend (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ DataDisplay (natural height, optional)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                         │
│ HorizontalBarGroup (flex: 1, fills)     │
│                                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartFooter (natural height)            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
       ↑                                ↑
       └────── Total height prop ───────┘
```

### Usage Examples

```tsx
// Fixed 500px chart - bar group fills remaining space
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  height={500}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={true}
/>

// Compact 280px chart for dashboards
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  height={280}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>

// Bars only - fills full height
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  height={300}
  chartHeader={false}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>
```

### Key Benefits

1. **Predictable sizing**: Chart always respects the specified height
2. **Automatic stretching**: Bar group expands to fill available space
3. **Consistent layouts**: Same chart height regardless of which sections are visible
4. **Responsive-friendly**: Use percentage heights for fluid layouts

### Auto-Collapse for Sparse Data (`autoHeight`)

When the dataset has only one or a few bars, the default fixed-height layout leaves the bars at the top of the bar-group area and the X-axis pinned to the bottom of the chart, with a large void in between. Set `autoHeight: true` to collapse the chart container to fit its content:

```tsx
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={[{ id: "total", category: "Total revenue", value: 850 }]}
  autoHeight
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabelOutside: true,
    rightLabelOutside: true,
    xAxis: true,
    barHeight: "XL",
  }}
/>
```

When `autoHeight: true`:

- The chart container's `height` prop is **ignored** — the container collapses to `header + legend + dataDisplay + bars + X-axis + footer` at their natural sizes
- The chart's `barGroupWrapper` switches from `flex: 1` to `flex: 0 0 auto` so the group doesn't stretch
- `HorizontalBarGroup.autoHeight: true` is forwarded so the group switches its `contentWrapper` to `flex: 0 0 auto + justify-content: flex-start` with a token-driven gap (`Dimensions/Spacings/3`) between bars — the X-axis sits immediately below the last bar

| Scenario                          | Use                                                                                             |
| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Single-bar / 2-3 bar sparse chart | **`autoHeight: true`** — chart collapses to fit; X-axis sits just below the bars                |
| Dense chart with many bars        | Leave `autoHeight: false` (default) — `space-between` distribution spreads bars across `height` |
| Fluid layout in a flex parent     | Leave `autoHeight: false` — pass `fullWidth` prop (or `height: "100%"`) instead                 |

See the `Edge Case - Single Bar` story in `HorizontalBarChart.stories.tsx` for the canonical example.

## Bar Overflow

The chart dynamically limits the number of visible bars to prevent overcrowding. Controlled by the `overflowType` prop in `barGroupConfig`.

### How It Works

The component measures the content area height via `ResizeObserver` and computes the maximum number of bars that fit while maintaining a minimum gap equal to **the bar height** between adjacent bars.

**Threshold rule**: `gap >= barHeight`

For N bars in a `space-between` layout:

```
gap = (contentHeight - N × barHeight) / (N - 1)
```

When the gap would fall below `barHeight`, the bottom bars are silently removed (no "Others" aggregation, no visual indicator).

### Overflow Types

| Type          | Behaviour                                                                        |
| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `"truncated"` | (Default) Bars that don't fit are removed from the bottom                        |
| `"all"`       | Every bar is rendered regardless of available space (preserves legacy behaviour) |

### Interaction with Sorting

Sorting (`dataSort`) is applied **before** truncation. With `dataSort: "desc"`, the highest-value bars remain visible and the smallest are truncated.

### Usage Examples

```tsx
// Default: bars automatically truncated when they don't fit
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  height={300}
  barGroupConfig={{
    barHeight: "M",
  }}
/>

// Show all bars regardless of space (no truncation)
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  height={300}
  barGroupConfig={{
    overflowType: "all",
  }}
/>
```

## Hover Interaction

The chart supports hover interaction with automatic dimming of non-hovered bars. `HorizontalBarGroup` automatically extends each bar's hit area to eliminate dead zones between bars — see [HorizontalBarGroup Hit Area Extension](./HorizontalBarGroup.md#hit-area-extension) for details.

### Color & Opacity States

| State                              | Color Token                      | Opacity | Description                   |
| ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------- |
| **Default** (nothing hovered)      | `categorical/bold/{colorIndex}`  | `1`     | Original vibrant colors       |
| **Highlighted** (this bar hovered) | `categorical/bold/{colorIndex}`  | `1`     | Stays vibrant                 |
| **Dimmed** (another bar hovered)   | `categorical/hover/{colorIndex}` | `0.2`   | Muted color + reduced opacity |

### Transition Tokens

All hover transitions use design tokens from the `hoverAnimation` collection:

- **Easing**: `"easing"` - Cubic-bezier timing function
- **Duration**: `"duration"` - Transition time (e.g., 200ms for "Moderate" mode)
- **Dim Opacity**: `"dimOpacity"` - Opacity for dimmed bars (default: 0.2)

```tsx
<HorizontalBarChart
  data={data}
  interactive={true}
  barGroupConfig={{
    onBarHover: (hoverData) => {
      if (hoverData.isHovered) {
        console.log(`Hovering: ${hoverData.label} - ${hoverData.value}`);
      }
    },
    onBarClick: (clickData) => {
      console.log(`Clicked: ${clickData.label}`);
    },
  }}
/>
```

